KZ3 patch 1136 (SPU pass 112): host threads that run SPU code (spu_async_thread = the Bink decoder, the SPURS kernel,
lane, policy-module and job-chain threads) are restricted to the highest efficiency class's logical processors on a
hybrid CPU (kz3_spu_thread_sched, runtime/spu/kz3_spu_sched.h; a no-op on a uniform CPU; KZ3_SPU_PCORES=0 = off). The default restricts only the spu_async_thread job
threads (the decoder), through the affinity mask; =all also the SPURS kernel, lane,
pm and jc threads (pass 112 A/B: worse on 1% low and frame-time spread), =sets uses CPU sets (Proton leaked 1 window in 2 of 3 runs). Pass 112
measured the Bink decoder at 570 ms/s on a P-core, 650-810 with a busy SMT sibling and 830-870 on an E-core, and the
scheduler left it on E-cores for seconds at a time: no margin, the loading-screen stall. Upstream candidate (general:
any recomp with SPU work on a hybrid CPU).

